      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "The prominent management law was that of Peter, he says the basic task of management includes both \nmarketing and innovation. According to him “Management is a Multi-purpose order that manages a business \nand manages managers and workers and work.” \n\nHarold Koontz defined management as the art of getting things done through with people in formally\norganized groups. \n\nManagement is the process of planning, organizing, leading and controlling an organization human, financial, \nphysical and information resources to achieve organizational goals in an efficient and effective manner.\n\nThe principle of management are the means by which a manager actually manages i.e. get things done through \nothers individually in groups or in organizations.\n\nFormally defined: The principle of management are the activities that plan, organize and control the opera-\ntions of the basic activities of people, materials, machines, methods, money and markets providing direction \nand coordination and giving leadership for human efforts so as to achieve the sought objectives of the \nenterprise.\n\nManagement when practice is definitely an art but it's underline applications methods and principles are a \nscience.\n\nBasic Component of Management\n• Management: An art and a Science\n• Evolution of Management: Various schools of thoughts\n• Function of Management\n• Concept of Organization\n",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "The prominent management law was that of Peter, he says the basic task of management includes both \nmarketing and innovation. According to him “Management is a Multi-purpose order that manages a business \nand manages managers and workers and work.” \n\nHarold Koontz defined management as the art of getting things done through with people in formally\norganized groups. \n\nManagement is the process of planning, organizing, leading and controlling an organization human, financial, \nphysical and information resources to achieve organizational goals in an efficient and effective manner.\n\nThe principle of management are the means by which a manager actually manages i.e. get things done through \nothers individually in groups or in organizations.\n\nFormally defined: The principle of management are the activities that plan, organize and control the opera-\ntions of the basic activities of people, materials, machines, methods, money and markets providing direction \nand coordination and giving leadership for human efforts so as to achieve the sought objectives of the \nenterprise.\n\nManagement when practice is definitely an art but it's underline applications methods and principles are a \nscience.\n\nBasic Component of Management\n• Management: An art and a Science\n• Evolution of Management: Various schools of thoughts\n• Function of Management\n• Concept of Organization\n",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
